  "details": "This is hard to word, but sometimes when I try to test/show off my showcase animations (that are keyframe timed), I occasionally get a lag spike from another player activating a toxic animation or someone just spawning into the world. What this does is delay the sound from the keyframe by a couple seconds, making the animation off beat.. I could easily go into a private world to fix this problem, but I like to present some animations in public worlds as well.\n\nI’m just curious on if it’s even possible to modify how lag occurs in the game to where the sound/keyframe doesn’t fuck up when a lag spike happens. Merci!",
